 me  [Music]  i grew up eating short ribs oxtails  raised lamb i always felt like it was  missing something until i fell in love  with the ingredient cinnamon and once i  put that in my short rib or my oxtails  or my braised lamb  it was incredible so i'm sharing that  with you that's the secret ingredient  here food became part of my dna through  my grandmother in really early age of  life but my grandmother made food look  really fun  so instead of me watching cartoons i was  in the kitchen cooking so this braising  technique  is a traditional braising technique it  has red wine in it but my flavor profile  in here is based for my travel so a  little bit of orange juice cinnamon  stick thyme bay leaf jalapeno so i'm  mixing it up a little bit  so foo can teach you about culture and  sometimes you don't need to travel  somewhere to learn about the culture of  that place so if you're thinking about  going somewhere go eat at a restaurant  that you think represents that place  and that food will start to tell you  about that culture i mean when i travel  or my friends travel or my family  travels the first thing you talk about  is where are we going to go eat what are  we going to do and it always is around  food in that place  the world loves rice because it's like a  field trip  it bounces it moves it goes in all these  different places this is how people move  and if you really look at rice  you'll see that certain cultures eat  certain races  sticky rice today you're taking a trip  into southeast asia  rice is  culture across the board it fuels  communities doesn't matter how much  money you have in your bank account we  all eat rice it connects everybody this  is the perfect dish to bring to any of  your holiday parties if you really want  to show off come on take a bite with me  look at that  rice's culture baby  [Music]  you
 

